/**
 * @file architecture.dox
 * @author Alexandru ALEXANDRESCU
 * @brief System Architecture Documentation
 * 
 * @page ArchitecturePage System Architecture Overview
 * @brief Event-driven, multi-threaded service architecture
 *
 * ## Overview
 * The architecture is built around:
 * - @ref EventPage "Event" — main event type - `Core::Event`
 * - @ref EventManagerPage "Event Manager" — central event dispatcher - `Core::EventManager`
 * - @ref ServiceBaseQueuePage "ServiceBaseQueue" — base class for thread-isolated asynchronous services - `Core::ServiceBaseQueue`
 * - @ref ServiceBasePage "ServiceBase" — base class for basic synchronous services that run in the same thread - `Core::ServiceBase`
 * - @ref ServiceManagerPage "Service Manager" — registry and lifecycle manager for services - `Core::ServiceManager`
 *
 * This structure enforces decoupling, thread-safety, and predictable startup/shutdown order.
 *
 * ## Ownership & Lifetime
 * - **EventManager**
 *   - Must outlive all services.
 *   - Centralized dispatcher; owns no threads.
 * - **ServiceManager**
 *   - Owns all service shared_ptrs and their threads.
 *   - Must outlive services’ execution.
 * - **Services (ServiceBaseQueue-derived)**
 *   - Always created via `std::make_shared`.
 *   - Never stack-allocated or manually `new` without shared ownership.
 *   - Must subscribe to events in `init()` only.
 *
 * ## Startup Sequence
 * 1. Create `EventManager` instance
 * 2. Create `ServiceManager` instance
 * 3. Create services via `std::make_shared` and register with ServiceManager
 *    - `init()` called
 *    - `start()` called
 *    - Service thread launched via `run()`
 * 4. Start UI or other layers
 *
 * ```text
 * EventManager
 *    |
 *    +--> ServiceManager
 *           |
 *           +--> ServiceA (thread)
 *           +--> ServiceB (thread)
 *           ...
 *    +--> UI / other layers
 * ```
 *
 * ## Shutdown Sequence
 * 1. Stop UI loop
 * 2. Stop `EventManager` (no more dispatch)
 * 3. `ServiceManager::stopAll()`
 *    - Signals `stop()` to each service
 *    - Joins all service threads
 * 4. Destroy services, ServiceManager, EventManager
 *
 * ## Threading Rules
 * - Each service runs in its own thread.
 * - Event dispatching happens in EventManager thread.
 * - `onEvent()` runs in EventManager thread; must be non-blocking.
 * - `dispatch()` runs in service thread; must not block queue mutex.
 * - `dispatchLoop()` must never block.
 * - Non-blocking and blocking dispatch loops provided (`dispatchLoop()` / `dispatchLoopBlocking()`).
 *
 * ## Event & Service Constraints
 * - Services communicate only via events; no direct calls.
 * - Each event type has a maximum number of subscribers.
 * - `ServiceId` and `EventType` enums must be contiguous.
 * - Maximum limits enforced via static arrays (`max_services`, `max_events`).
 *
 * ## Notes
 * - No detached threads allowed.
 * - Services must not assume dispatch order.
 * - Events are processed opportunistically; immediate processing is not guaranteed.
 * - Critical services should start before others if startup dependencies exist.
 *
 */